# Revisions that changed formatting only, and should be skipped by `git blame`.
#
# A commit belongs here when it changed no behaviour: it was produced by a
# formatter or another mechanical rewrite, it touched many files, and every
# line it moved still has a meaningful author in the commit before it. Without
# this list those commits become the blame answer for a large part of the tree
# and the real authorship becomes one `git blame` hop further away each time.
#
# Enable it locally, once per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Forges that read this file (GitHub, GitLab) apply it to their blame views
# without any configuration. `git blame --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs`
# works ad hoc if you would rather not set the config.
#
# Add entries newest-last, each with the command that produced it. An entry is
# only honest if a reader can re-run that command and get the same tree.

